---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'About slipfallcalculator.com';
const description = 'About the team behind slipfallcalculator.com — free slip and fall settlement calculators and plain-English premises liability guides.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>About slipfallcalculator.com</h1>

  <p>slipfallcalculator.com is a free personal injury resource maintained by The Click Lab. Our calculator and guides help people understand how slip and fall settlement values are estimated, what factors affect outcomes, and what steps to take after an injury. The site covers the full arc of a premises liability claim &mdash; from documenting the scene on the day of the fall to understanding what a final settlement number reflects.</p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>We translate complex legal and financial concepts into plain-English tools. Our settlement calculator applies the multiplier method used by insurance adjusters and plaintiff attorneys to give you an educational estimate of what a claim might be worth, with full transparency about the formulas involved. Our <a href="/guides/">guide library</a> covers the step-by-step claims process, liability standards by property type, post-fall action steps, and common misconceptions that cause people to undervalue or mishandle their claims.</p>
  <p>Every page is written and reviewed by our <a href="/editorial/">editorial team</a> against primary legal sources before publication, and updated when law or industry practice changes. We aim to be the most accurate free resource on this topic, not just the most visible one.</p>

  <h2>What we don&rsquo;t do</h2>
  <p>We do not provide legal advice, and nothing on this site creates an attorney-client relationship. Calculator results are educational estimates &mdash; they do not predict the outcome of any specific case. Premises liability law varies significantly by state, and a general-purpose tool cannot capture every jurisdiction-specific nuance. For guidance on your situation, consult a licensed personal injury attorney in your state. Most offer free initial consultations for injury claims.</p>
  <p>Our editorial guides and calculator do not recommend specific law firms or accept paid placements, and our editorial decisions are independent of our advertising relationships.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>slipfallcalculator.com is supported by Google AdSense display advertising. Ads are served automatically based on page content and visitor context &mdash; we do not sell or share reader data for advertising purposes. We also offer an optional case-review form on the homepage: if you submit it, your name, phone, email, and case details are shared with attorneys who may compensate The Click Lab Agency LLC for the referral. That's a separate, disclosed product from our editorial content, and using it is always optional. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for full details on data practices, including exactly what's shared if you use that form.</p>

  <h2>Who maintains this site</h2>
  <p>slipfallcalculator.com is owned and operated by The Click Lab, a boutique online publishing business focused on high-accuracy utility sites in legal and financial niches. The editorial team includes premises liability practice and contributing research expertise. More information about our team and editorial process is on the <a href="/editorial/">editorial page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions, corrections, or feedback: see our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We read every message. We cannot respond to requests for legal advice or case-specific analysis.</p>
</BaseLayout>
